From ea94e22b790981588e1b858b2bbcf123812aa969 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:34:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Bluetooth: hci_qca: do not touch a closed serdev port on
 shutdown

qca_power_shutdown() sets the baud rate and sends a power pulse through
the serdev port. Both need that port open, and it is only open between
hci_uart_open() and hci_uart_close(). host_set_baudrate() checks that
hu->serdev exists, which it does from probe onward, but not that it is
open; ttyport_set_baudrate() then dereferences serport->tty, which is
only set while the port is open.

A controller that never completes setup leaves hci0 down, so the port is
never opened. Removing the driver reaches qca_power_shutdown() from
qca_serdev_remove() and oopses:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference
  pc : tty_set_termios+0x28/0x3dc
  lr : ttyport_set_baudrate+0x74/0xa0
  Call trace:
    ttyport_set_baudrate
    serdev_device_set_baudrate
    qca_power_shutdown [hci_uart]
    qca_serdev_remove [hci_uart]

Skip the two operations that need an open port, and keep disabling the
regulators, which is what actually has to happen on the way down.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
index 4cff4d9be3132..976f099fcb1ba 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -2208,8 +2208,18 @@ static void qca_power_shutdown(struct hci_uart *hu)
 	case QCA_WCN3990:
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
 	case QCA_WCN3998:
-		host_set_baudrate(hu, 2400);
-		qca_send_power_pulse(hu, false);
+		/* Both of these talk to the serdev port, and the port is only
+		 * open between hci_uart_open() and hci_uart_close().
+		 * ttyport_set_baudrate() dereferences the tty behind it
+		 * without checking, so a controller that never came up -- the
+		 * port never opened -- takes the baud rate change through a
+		 * NULL tty and oopses on driver removal. The rails still have
+		 * to come down either way.
+		 */
+		if (test_bit(HCI_UART_PROTO_READY, &hu->flags)) {
+			host_set_baudrate(hu, 2400);
+			qca_send_power_pulse(hu, false);
+		}
 		qca_regulator_disable(qcadev);
 		break;
 
